## Executive Summary

Built a **professional CI/CD pipeline** that automates infrastructure deployment using GitHub Actions and Terraform. The pipeline validates code changes on pull requests, deploys infrastructure to AWS with approval gates, and provides comprehensive visibility into all deployments.

This system eliminates manual infrastructure changes, prevents configuration errors from reaching production, and provides audit trails of all deployments — hallmarks of enterprise-grade infrastructure management.

---

## The Problem Solved

### Before This Phase

Infrastructure management was manual and error-prone:
- ❌ Running `terraform apply` locally without validation
- ❌ No visibility into what changes were being made
- ❌ Risk of human error breaking production
- ❌ No audit trail of who deployed what when
- ❌ Deployment process wasn't standardized
- ❌ Credentials stored insecurely

### After This Phase

Infrastructure deployment is automated, validated, and secure:
- ✅ Every code change automatically validated before deployment
- ✅ Changes reviewed by team via GitHub PR comments
- ✅ Production deployments require manual approval
- ✅ Complete audit trail in GitHub Actions logs
- ✅ Standardized deployment process
- ✅ No credentials stored (OIDC authentication)

