### 3. **Comprehensive Variable Management**

**Challenge:**
- Terraform needs values to run (domain names, instance types, etc.)
- Values shouldn't be hardcoded
- Sensitive values must stay private
- CI/CD needs to access values

**Solution: Two-File System**

```
LOCAL DEVELOPMENT:
  terraform.tfvars (gitignored)
  ├── Contains actual values
  ├── Private to your computer
  └── Used: terraform apply locally

GITHUB REPOSITORY:
  example.tfvars (committed to git)
  ├── Contains same values (safe to commit)
  ├── Public in repository
  └── Used: GitHub Actions CI/CD

VALUES MATCH:
  Both files have identical values
  ├── Local development works
  ├── CI/CD automation works
  └── No value mismatches
```

**Variables Provided to Workflows:**
```yaml
aws_region: us-east-1
instance_type: t3.micro
key_name: hng-infrastructure
domain_name: infra.mosesekerin.name.ng
parent_domain: mosesekerin.name.ng
vpc_cidr: 10.0.0.0/16
public_subnet_cidr: 10.0.1.0/24
hng_username: Timileyin-Your-SRE-Guy
letsencrypt_email: mosesekerin@gmail.com
allowed_ssh_cidrs: ["102.93.7.11/32"]
enable_dns: true
```

