### 5. **Error Prevention & Safety**

**Validation Layers:**

```
Layer 1: Local Development
├─ terraform validate (syntax)
├─ terraform fmt (formatting)
├─ terraform plan (preview)
└─ Manual review before commit

Layer 2: Pull Request (plan.yml)
├─ terraform fmt -check (formatting enforced)
├─ terraform validate (syntax)
├─ terraform plan (infrastructure preview)
├─ Automated PR comment
└─ Merge blocked if errors

Layer 3: Deployment (apply.yml)
├─ terraform plan (final check)
├─ Manual approval required
├─ terraform apply (only after approval)
└─ Audit logged to GitHub

Layer 4: GitHub
├─ Branch protection on main
├─ PR reviews required
└─ Status checks must pass
```

**Real Example: Detecting Errors**

Scenario: Developer has syntax error in code
```
Developer writes: var.instance_typ (typo)
                  Should be: var.instance_type

Local test:
  terraform validate → Error: Variable "instance_typ" not found

Push to GitHub:
  plan.yml → ❌ Validation failed
  PR shows: ❌ Checks failed (red X)
  Merge blocked ← Can't merge until fixed

Developer fixes:
  Corrects to: var.instance_type
  Push again → plan.yml → ✅ Passes
  PR shows: ✅ Checks passed (green ✓)
  Can now merge
```

